Reconstruct FUN_0000_1caf (resource word-copy) -- dynamic-DS rep-movsw source base loss.

asm (base-0 0x1caf):
  push ds; mov di,ds; mov es,di; mov ds,ax          ; ES=DGROUP, DS=param_1 (source segment)
  mov cx,[ds:0]; xor si,si; mov di,0x3af0            ; count = word at param_1:0; dest DGROUP:0x3af0
  shr cx,1; shr cx,1; adc cx,cx                      ; cx = (count>>2)*2 + ((count>>1)&1)
  rep movsw ds:si -> es:di; pop ds; ret

FUN_0000_1caf(param_1) copies N=(count>>2)*2+((count>>1)&1) words from segment param_1:0 to
DGROUP:0x3af0, where count is the leading word at param_1:0. Reached on the boot path via
app_entry -> FUN_0000_1c6a -> FUN_0000_1cdb -> 1caf(0x2be9) (a resource/table load). Ghidra dropped
the DS=param_1 source base of the rep-movsw (the string-op segment-context class, cf. patches
006/010/014) so the source pointer AND the count read collapsed to host address 0 (`*(uint*)0x0`) ->
SIGSEGV. Rebased the source to g_mem+(param_1<<4); the dest DGROUP:0x3af0 (= &DAT_1000_faf0) was
already correct.
